\v 2 Then Mosheh \add !(Moses)\add* called all Yisrael together and told them, “You've all seen¦96082 everything that¦96081 Yahweh did to Far-oh and all his servants in Egypt and \add ≡what he did\add* to all his country \add ≈right in front of¦96083\add* your¦96083 eyes¦96083—
\v 3 the sufferings \add of the people there\add* that¦96104 you saw¦96099 for¦96095 yourselves, along with the incredible miracles,
\v 4 \add ≈yet up until now\add*, Yahweh¦96107 hasn't enabled you all to understand¦96121 the meaning of¦96115 everything that you saw and¦96117 heard.
\v 5 For¦96135 forty years, \add ≈Yahweh¦96136\add* led you all in the wilderness, \add but\add* your clothes didn't¦96126 wear through, and¦96128 the sandals on your feet never wore out.
\v 6 You all \add survived without\add* bread to¦96141 eat or any wine or alcohol to¦96154 drink so that you'd realise that I am your god Yahweh.
\v 7 Then when we¦96159 arrived here, King Sihon from Heshbon and¦96163 King Og from Bashan came out \add ≈to¦96165 battle\add* against us, \add ≈but¦96159 we¦96163 defeated them\add*.\x + \xo 29:7: a \xt Num 21:21-30; \xo b \xt Num 21:31-35.\x*
