\v 26 and they went and served other gods and bowed down to¦96555 them—gods that¦96562 they hadn't \add ≈heard of¦96559 before or had anything to do with¦96563\add*.
\v 27 That's why Yahweh¦96568 was angry¦96572 at¦96571 that¦96581 country and¦96567 brought all the¦96581 curses written in¦96571 this¦96581 scroll onto it—
\v 28 tearing them away from their land \add ≈in his raging anger\add*, and¦96587 threw them into another land as \add we can see\add* today.’
\p
\v 29 Our god Yahweh \add ≈has his secrets\add*, \add ≈but what he's revealed\add* is for us and our children forever, so that we can follow all his instructions.
